<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Chester</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a> was a British army officer who served as governor of the Province of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> from 1770 until its capture by Spanish forces in 1781. He governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pensacola">Pensacola</a> alongside an elected assembly, with which he often quarrelled. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a> the colony became a refuge for loyalists before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-de-galvez">Bernardo de Gálvez</a> took Pensacola in 1781.</p></div>
